Why this is a separate file
---------------------------

LICENSE is the verbatim GPL-2.0 text. The only

    Copyright (C) <year>  <name of author>

line in it belongs to the licence's own "How to Apply These Terms to Your New
Programs" appendix. That is an example intended to be copied into your own
files -- not a blank to be filled in inside the licence. Editing it would
modify the licence text itself, which is not something a licensee should do.

GPL-2.0 section 1 expects each source file to carry a notice. Per-file headers
are deliberately not used here: this fork tracks an active upstream, and a
header added to every file would conflict with essentially any future upstream
change. The same reasoning keeps stylistic lint rules off (see ruff.toml) and
keeps every pre-commit hook read-only.

A single file naming the holder of this fork's changes is the version of that
notice which survives an upstream sync.

See issue #7.
